      "message": "refactor(sim): the field column read from below - march_up, the mirrored sliver law, the shell-crossing read (#637 E2b)\n\n`SdfField::column_span` reads a column from both sides. The top stays\n`march`'s descent; the floor is `march_up`'s ascent (new `march_up.rs`,\nthe mirror of `march`/`refine`: same keyed probe and budgets, descending\nto the LOWEST material centre and reading the floor from `cut_downs` -\na flipped bake's `cut_ups` records moved whole - or the shell's lowest\ncrossing in the bracket, the higher binding). A field with no\n`cut_downs` keeps E1's monotone law with no ascent, so the upright path\nis byte-identical in value and cost.\n\nBoth marches now read an uncut surface from the cached parity column's\ncrossing inside the bracket (`march::shell_in`, `march::face`) instead\nof the cell boundary, exact to rounding for any plane - a flipped stock\nbottom is not lattice-aligned in general. A sign flip with neither a\ncrossing nor a record (a flipped bounded tool's bottom face) is\n`Unreadable`, never the boundary as a guess; on an upright field it\ncannot occur (every proven-inside cell records entry 0, and the cell\nunder it a finite entry).\n\nThe sliver law (no material centre) is one scan over adjacent air-centre\npairs from the cell under the shell floor to the one over its ceiling:\nthe lower centre's `cut_ups` entry is the upper cut's bottom, the upper\ncentre's `cut_downs` entry is the lower cut's top, the shell binds where\nno record does, and a centre proven inside a cut is that cut's whole\nhalf-line. It reads E1's floor sliver, its mirror under a flipped cut,\nand a sliver floating between a cut from below and one from above.\n\nE2a's interim refusal (`bounded_cuts` on a flipped bake) is lifted; the\nflag follows the tool alone. `floor_at` keeps its API. Column-engine\nverdicts, goldens and snapshots are unchanged.\n\nPinned by field_floor (the exact read where the interim refusal was\npinned, the flipped through-slot, the mirrored sliver, the flipped\nbounded tool's refusal, an unaligned plane read on both sides) and\ncarry_engine_agreement (the baked read-back bit-for-bit with the view\nthrough all 8 turns, flips included; an unaligned block top; the slots\ncut before and after a flip - two-sided columns, a sliver between the\ntwo cuts, a cut through the first - agreeing with the column engine per\ncolumn to 1e-6).\n\nFixes #780\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
