  {
    "sha": "3fa2631c0f65cff2d18dacc8dd168ada2379e493",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKDNmYTI2MzFjMGY2NWNmZjJkMThkYWNjOGRkMTY4YWRhMjM3OWU0OTM",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-11T09:50:44Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-11T09:50:44Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(sim): a level facet's ray crossing is exactly its height\n\n`plane_claim` read a crossing as the barycentric sum\n`(1 - u - v) a.z + u b.z + v c.z`, which rounds by an ulp on some rays\neven when the facet's three z are equal: the stepped facing golden's\nuncut columns at y -6.25 read a stock top of 2.0 + 1 ulp, and the\nrest ladder's strict `above(2.0)` mask disagreed with the column\nengine there once the field read an uncut surface from its shell\ncrossing (#780) instead of the cell boundary that was exact by\naccident. A facet whose three z are equal now answers that z, bit for\nbit; a tilted facet keeps the sum. E1's floor on the same columns\nreads -638.0 instead of -638.0000000000001.\n\nCaught by app's heavy `stock_engine_agreement` lane (release), green\nwith this. Pinned by\nsolid_rest::tests::a_level_facet_crosses_at_exactly_its_height.\n\nRefs #780\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
