  {
    "sha": "dc4873e74ece40e9aacab493b0d39f08686f7fa7",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKGRjNDg3M2U3NGVjZTQwZTlhYWNhYjQ5M2IwZDM5ZjA4Njg2ZjdmYTc",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-11T10:47:12Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-11T10:47:12Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(sim): the field marches walk cell centres with exact signs, never points\n\nThe review of PR #817 found march_up's `phi == 0 => Floor(z)` exit (a copy\nof march's) reading a flipped floor 0.25 high: a probe's magnitude is the\ncell's, so a cell whose centre lies on a stock plane reads zero at every\npoint of the cell, and the exit answered whatever height the ascent had\nreached. The same exit stands upright in march (#824). Two more holes\nshare the root in both marches: the sphere trace stepped by the cell's\nmagnitude from points between centres (a band value can over-read the\ntruth by up to sqrt(3) cells), so it could land past a web thinner than\na cell; and its \"last air probe\" fallback was no proof under a cut claim.\n\nOne shared `march::walk` now visits cell centres only, with the exact\nparity-and-claim sign at each (the half-open [floor, top) law: a centre\non a floor plane is material, on a top plane air), skips only runs the\nfield proves air (a centre outside the shell: its magnitude's cells less\ntwo; a claimed centre: its claim's cells), and reads the surface at the\nfirst material centre from the one-cell bracket to the proven-air centre\nbefore it (`face`, unchanged). `march` and `march_up` are the two\ndirections of that walk; `refine`, `refine_down`, `probe`, `STEP_MIN`\nand `MAX_MARCH_STEPS` are gone. The sliver scan's upper bound follows\nthe same law (a centre on the ceiling is the one above it), so the\nreviewer's scenario reads [5.8, 6.25] exactly through the record.\n\nPinned by field_floor::a_stock_plane_on_a_cell_centre_reads_exactly_on_both_sides\n(the reviewer's flipped scenario, #824's upright twin, the uncut plate\nboth ways, a top on a centre) and\nfield_floor::no_column_under_reports_across_plates_and_slots_on_and_off_the_lattice\n(4 floors x 3 tops x 9 slot depths, under and beside the slot, upright\nand flipped: 432 reads, all exact, none under-read). Both fail on the\nold marches. Every existing suite reads the same floats; the app's\nrelease heavy lane agrees with the column engine on every golden.\n\nRefs #780\nRefs #824\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
