  {
    "sha": "03437938a1e013ec19a82ab515523ab0fca7a5d7",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKDAzNDM3OTM4YTFlMDEzZWMxOWE4MmFiNTE1NTIzYWIwZmNhN2E1ZDc",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-11T11:18:41Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-11T11:18:41Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(sim): a centre-less floor skin is a verdict on every march path, never NaN\n\nThe second review of #817 found that `march::walk` answered `NoMaterial`\nfor a column whose remaining skin held no cell centre (a plate -6.05..0\nat cell 0.5 with a slot at -5.8 leaves [-6.05, -5.8] between the air\ncentre at -6.25 and the claimed centre at -5.75). Every verdict reader\nthat marches alone - `Stock::top`, `deviate`, `measure`, the sheet and\nthe column masks - read that as NaN: the rest under the slot vanished\nfrom the report and the rest mask would have treated the steel as air.\nOnly `column_span` read such skins, through `field_floor`'s sliver law.\n\nThe walk now reads a centre-less column itself before it ever answers\n\"no material\", through the one sliver law (`field_floor::sliver`, shared,\nwith the shell's extent from the new `shell_extent`): a column the shell\nnever crosses is air, a sliver the records place answers its top (a\ndescent) or floor (an ascent), one the records prove cut through is\n`NoMaterial`, and one that cannot be placed is `Unreadable` - never\n`NoMaterial` where the shell says material stands. The mesh-only walk\nanswers the shell's highest or lowest crossing. `column_span`'s own\n`NoMaterial => sliver` arm becomes `Empty`.\n\nPinned by the new `field_skin` suite: the reviewer's scenario through\n`Stock::top`, `deviate` (192 of 192 columns rest, 0 NaN), `Columns` and\nthe flipped stock; and a sweep of 6 floors x 3 tops x 12 slot depths\n(skins 0.01-0.3), upright and flipped, through `Stock::top`, the flipped\n`column_span` and `deviate` - 1296 reads, 1296 exact, no NaN, no refusal\n(186 NaN reads and 81 NaN deviate runs on the previous head). Both pins\nfail on the unfixed source; the round-1 pins stay green.\n\nRefs #780\nRefs #824\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
