  {
    "sha": "8ed831b7a8b14d99d42e05fb05338013c420e20b",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKDhlZDgzMWI3YThiMTRkOTlkNDJlMDVmYjA1MzM4MDEzYzQyMGUyMGI",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-11T11:57:48Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-11T11:57:48Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(sim): cuts through a carried field in the new frame (#637 E2c)\n\nCarriedField::simulate bakes the view's signed permutation into the\nbricks (SdfField::turned) on the first cut after a turn, shifts every\nmove by the residual translation (from, to, and the arc centre in its\nplane's word order) and cuts through simulate_field - the field arm of\nStock::simulate moved into one function, so later cuts ride the shipped\n+Z tool construction (spanning_flank, batched per brick): true XY arcs,\nthe closed-form flat floor. The clip stays at read-back; column_body\nreads through column_span.\n\nCarriedField keeps a sticky `flipped` flag (new, then): a baked flip\nleaves only a translation as the view, and two composed flips an upright\none, yet the floor has faced the spindle - Body::carry's own law.\n\ncarry_engine_agreement runs #780's by-hand cut-after-flip pins through\nthe real simulate and grows an XY arc after the flip and a second carry\n(quarter turn; flip back) after a cut; both engines agree per column on\nempty_at, top and floor to 1e-6 and on floor_judged. field_carry pins\nsimulate bit for bit against the by-hand bake and shift through all 8\nturns (XY and XZ arcs), the refusal-before-bake order, and the flag.\n\nFixes #781\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
